// GENERATED — do not edit by hand. Regenerate with tools/genBundledArt.py.
//
// Every piece of artwork in the app, as a static require(), keyed by the
// same filename utils/assetHost.js used to build a CDN URL from.
//
// WHY A LOOKUP TABLE AND NOT require() AT EACH CALL SITE (v0.9.2)
//
// Metro resolves require() at build time, so its argument has to be a
// literal it can see. Most call sites could have been rewritten one by
// one -- but data/brandArt.js builds the mascot poses in a loop:
//
//     acc[pose] = assetUri(MASCOT_POSE_FILES[pose]);
//
// There is no literal there to rewrite. A table keeps every require()
// static and literal where Metro needs it, and leaves the lookup dynamic
// where the app needs it, so that loop and every other caller is
// untouched. assetUri() consults this first and falls back to the CDN
// for anything not here, which is what lets a food added between App
// Store releases still draw.
//
// 1826 files, about 48.9 MB. That is the whole of the app's download size
// beyond the JS bundle, and the reason the first run no longer shows
// images arriving a beat late.

